From 0a6b8af1e40b7b20d167d1d70d2a16c074325c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:26:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Count item 3-8a's population, with an instrument made to
 discriminate

The first attempt at this counter read zero on all seven Octane suites
and was nearly reported as a zero, before anyone had shown it could read
anything else. It could not, and it was reverted. This one is built the
other way round: it is made to discriminate on constructed shapes first,
and only then pointed at the corpus.

AnalyzeSpeculative still works by difference against the real fixed
point rather than by a new rule -- run the same resolution a second time
with an identifier the function neither declares nor takes as a
parameter assumed numeric, and subtract the real survivors -- so the set
cannot drift from what the analysis actually does. Two fixes were needed
over the first attempt. The population needs a set of names the function
DECLARES, not just the ones it offered as candidates, or a local that
never qualified (`var a = []`) is mistaken for a name from outside the
function and assumed numeric. And the switch is a COMPILE-time one, so
the driver turns it on before the corpus is compiled rather than beside
the run-time censuses, which is where it went first.

Seven fixtures pin the discrimination, and the two that matter are
negatives: a local defeated by a Parameter is one slot away in the same
enum and must stay out, because a parameter is a value the caller picks
per call rather than a name from outside the function, and an instrument
that could not separate them would report this population as everything
item 3-3 already deferred; and the never-offered local above.

Counted on the corpus: 26 names, numeric locals 232 -> 258, 1.11x. The
distribution is the result rather than the total -- six suites gain one
to three names each, and NavierStokes gains fifteen, going 24 -> 39,
1.62x. That is the largest single-suite widening this phase has
produced, and it lands on the suite carrying 9.46 M of the 16.95 M
LocalSlot steps and 6.76 M of the 7.05 M real update boxes. For contrast
item 3-7 widened by 8 names at 1.036x and was worth 1.0001x, because its
eight were scattered where nothing hot lived.

The count does not license the build. The mechanism is still the XL
recorded with 0093: every fast path keys off NumericStorage and a
speculative local is a double only while a flag holds. What the count
settles is that the work would have something to reach.

Counter off by default; it costs a second analysis pass per compiled
function. No behaviour change.
